Z||000006||Carrolles||09-17-2001||07:58 AM||||Whenever you have to jump start a dead battery you should leave the charged battery connected to the dead one for a while to transfer as much charge to it as possible before you start the engine.  Otherwise you will risk Alternator Death.<P>Last year Kit Car Magazine (or maybe it was Kit Car Illustrated) had an excellent article on batteries.  It showed that when a battery is completely discharged (unless it is a deep cycle marine type battery) it loses approximately one half of its useful life.  They are not designed to withstand complete discharge unaffected.  Each time it gets completely discharged it loses half its remaining life.<P>So you could have fried your battery when your alternator died.<P>||||reg||1
