Z||000012||MD_Fiero||09-29-2001||10:28 PM||||dude, im in the SAME situation man!...<P><BR>i bet ur pissed...lets be pissed together....luckily for me...the alternater was replaced about 3 years ago, and i bought a new battery today..and everything work perfect =)<P>all last month for me..the car would start up with out hesitating,...then once i go to give it a run after setting for about 2=3 months..it wouldnt start...so i got pissed..jumped it..and worked...soon to die out 15-20 mins later..then jumped again, and brought home..and wouldnt start back up...so it sat some more..and today i went to buy a new battery and it works wonders...gave it a goooooood run today...loosened up the brake/gas pedal's since it sat..and it was the first time driving it/besides the school parking lot...so it was a little hard for me...but im happy now. and will be greatly use to it in a period of time....hope everything works out, let me know man!||||reg||1
Z||000013||ArchMagi||09-30-2001||03:10 AM||||I had the same problem about a month ago.  Keep on dyeing on me. Had alternator and battery checked, both good.<P>To cut a long story short, my problem was that water had entered my left tail lights and was causing the battery to short out, causing a CONSTANT drain on my battery.<P>Checking that out might be worth while.  I also bought some engine fog to spray on all my ground termals just to be sure.<P>------------------<BR>87 Coupe with 168,000KM<BR>4cyl, 5 speed||||reg||1
Z||000014||SKIDMARK||09-30-2001||08:09 AM||||Sounds like the battery to me too. I had a bad switch for the trunk light and it would drain the battery in a few days at first. By the time I figured it out, the battery wouldn't start the car, even after charging for overnight. Most decent parts stores can check your battery and charging system for free.||||reg||1
